    <strong>What to notice:</strong> commit to an answer before reading each
    explanation — every option is a property combination, not a fact to recall.
    Questions 1 and 4 test the same idea from two sides: the exponent in the index
    comes from the loading geometry, which is why translation matters. Question 2
    checks the log-log geometry behind the guideline lines; question 3 separates
    screening from ranking, the distinction the method leans on hardest.
  </p>
